  "decision": [
    "Reject eager whole-dictionary preparation as a universal default: 10000-entry dictionaries with 100 selected rows lose all eight cases in both runs.",
    "Keep direct access as the required low-memory fallback: all 144 exact-direct-cap cache trials reject while direct execution succeeds. A fit-only rule would also select slower caches in sparse high-cardinality cases.",
    "Small-dictionary preparation remains a credible optional/adaptive optimization: all 24 cases with 64 dictionary values win in each run.",
    "Do not infer a universal cardinality threshold from timing alone; one of 72 winners flips between runs. An adaptive production path must also respect selected work, ordering/monotonicity, currently available capacity and output overlap."
  ],
